{"content":[{"c":["ENAN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Ahira’s father. Ahira was appointed by Moses as the commander of the tribe of Naphtali during the first census of Israel in the desert of Sinai (",{"href":"?bref=Num.1.15","r":"Num.1.15","rawR":"Num.1.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.1.15","value":"Num.1.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 1:15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.2.29","r":"Num.2.29","rawR":"Num.2.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.2.29","value":"Num.2.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:29"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.7.78,83","r":"Num.7.78,83","rawR":"Num.7.78,83","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.7.78,83","value":"Num.7.78,83"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:78, 83"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.10.27","r":"Num.10.27","rawR":"Num.10.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.10.27","value":"Num.10.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:27"},"). The name is apparently preserved in the name Hazar-enan (-enon), a town somewhere between Damascus and Hauran (",{"href":"?bref=Num.34.9","r":"Num.34.9","rawR":"Num.34.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.34.9","value":"Num.34.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 34:9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.47.17","r":"Ezek.47.17","rawR":"Ezek.47.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.47.17","value":"Ezek.47.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 47:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.48.1","r":"Ezek.48.1","rawR":"Ezek.48.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.48.1","value":"Ezek.48.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"48:1"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Enan","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nm 1:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.1.15","rawQueryValue":"Num.1.15","sourceRefExact":"Num.1.15"},{"anchorText":"2:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.2.29","rawQueryValue":"Num.2.29","sourceRefExact":"Num.2.29"},{"anchorText":"7:78, 83","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bre